## Setup status — is this campaign runnable yet?

`new-campaign` hands off **launch-ready**: the FROZEN scorer and the experiment hooks are
implemented, `--selftest` passes, exp 000 has run and its floor is recorded, and the driver's preflight was
green at handoff (any exception — something only the user could stage — was handed over by name).
The authoritative answer is always mechanical, never a table to maintain:

```
python scripts/run_campaign.py --preflight --backend <codex|claude>
```

It refuses to launch while anything is missing and names each item with its fix — run it first on
any imported, relocated, or hand-built tree, which lacks all of the above by default. Downstream of a
first launch, the gates hold the rest: experiment 000 must measure the baseline and the trivial
reference before any comparison means anything, and promotion stays blocked until the correctness
suite is green and the noise model is confirmed empirically. Setup tasks preflight cannot know about
(data only the user can stage, an instrument to connect) live as the opening `results/JOURNAL.md`
**NEXT** line and `## What to try next and why` items — the loop's working list — not in a separate ledger.

